00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:45.000
Whitney Hodges: So…

00:46:46.000 --> 00:47:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Essentially, what happens when somebody goes to Google to search is that Google is going to show them your ad if they think that your ad is going to be relevant to them, if they think that there's going to be a high likelihood of them clicking on your ad.

00:47:02.000 --> 00:47:18.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, with Google Ads, it is pay-per-click, so you are only charged your ad spend if somebody actually clicks on the ad. Um, what is also really nice about the Google Ads is that we have complete control over.

00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:35.000
Whitney Hodges: what these ads are going to say, right? So, when your venue just shows up organically in the Google search results, Google's kind of just putting out there whatever it wants there to be, kind of based on what they've seen on the website, what the copy is on the website.

