00:51:35.000 --> 00:51:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, exactly. So where these are meant to show up are going to be like, you know, in stories placements. So on Facebook and Instagram, if you're scrolling through stories, ads can pop up there. So video ads, like real style ads can work really well there.

00:51:53.000 --> 00:52:09.000
Whitney Hodges: And then, of course, just like, you know, as you're scrolling the newsfeed. So, it's a bit different than Google Ads, right? Because with Google, people are going to search, it's high intent, you know, they're specifically looking for, you know, a venue. Whereas when people.

00:52:01.000 --> 00:52:02.000
judy: Okay.

00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:26.000
Whitney Hodges: hop onto Instagram or Facebook for the most part. They're going there to just kind of like scroll to be entertained, or maybe it's to connect with friends and family things like that. So this would be considered more disruptor marketing, right? Because what we want to do is.

00:52:18.000 --> 00:52:19.000
judy: Okay.

00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:42.000
Whitney Hodges: get in front of the people on those platforms where we can capture their attention, you know, pique their curiosity, kind of disrupt what they're already doing to make them aware and to get them to click through, essentially.

00:52:43.000 --> 00:53:02.000
Whitney Hodges: And so, um, we can do a variety of different things with the meta ads, which is really exciting. We call it a full funnel of ads, because we can reach completely cold audiences, we can reach, um, you know, your warmer audiences, but then we can also set up retargeting ads, which we would consider to be.

00:53:02.000 --> 00:53:19.000
Whitney Hodges: um, you know, your hottest audience members. So, if you've ever experienced, like, you know, Googling something, or going to somebody's website, and then opening up your Facebook or Instagram, and then you very quickly thereafter see an ad.

00:53:19.000 --> 00:53:48.000
Whitney Hodges: For that business, that is retargeting. So that's one of the things that we would do, right? We know that, you know, couples or brides, as they're researching, as they're checking things out, they may hit your website and they may not be ready to inquire or ready to book a tour. They may just kind of be researching. So then when they open up their social media apps and see you again, it's like a reminder, right? It's continuing them on that journey. It's building that, like, know, like, trust factor.

00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:34.000
judy: Oh, okay.

00:53:48.000 --> 00:53:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and so it's helping the ads on each platform really kind of work together, and to help compound the results.

00:53:58.000 --> 00:54:20.000
Whitney Hodges: So, what we like to do here, and this is different than, I would say, um, you know, a lot of agencies, or even, you know, what some other, you know, ads managers do, is we like to run a variety of different ads, um, all at once. And it's for those different purposes, right? Because what somebody needs to see who has never heard of Pecan Springs Ranch before.

00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:11.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:36.000
Whitney Hodges: is very different than what somebody we would want to show somebody who has already explored the website. Right? So we write different ad copy. We craft different creatives for those different purposes. So, you know, you can see here that really none of these ads are the same. It's all.

00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:24.000
judy: Mm-hmm.

00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:53.000
Whitney Hodges: different copy, it's different videos that we've used. Oftentimes, we will leverage some of your existing Instagram content, and then we can turn that into an ad, right? So if you have a really great reel that showcases a really nice wedding, well, we may, you know, grab that.

00:54:53.000 --> 00:55:00.000
